{"summary": "Two distinct advice topics discussed:

1. CONTAINER GARDENING: User received advice on watering (finger test - 1 inch into soil; every 1-2 days in summer, weekly in cooler months), soil (avoid yard dirt - use potting mix or cactus mix for succulents, costs are low), and perennial plant recommendations (lavender, sedum, daylilies, hostas for shade). Assistant emphasized drainage holes are critical - sitting in water kills plants, not underwatering. User was advised to check USDA hardiness zone before buying.

2. TODDLER EATING & SLEEP: User's 3-year-old refuses green foods and sometimes meat. Assistant advised against forcing tastes - can create negative associations. Recommended: pair familiar foods with tiny new bites (1 tsp portions), repeated exposure without pressure (10-15 tries), making food fun (shapes, dipping in hummus), involving child in cooking. User noted child loves helping in kitchen. For sleep training, Assistant suggested consistent 30-minute routine (bath, book, song, lights out same order), brief check-ins every 5 minutes if child cries, noting most kids adjust within a week."}
